1
00:00:01,670 --> 00:00:09,570
(Transcribed by TurboScribe. Go Unlimited to remove this message.) How do we reach a high level in

2
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:12,170
training and learning any skill?

3
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:15,410
How does it happen that we achieve a high level

4
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:17,650
in what truly matters to us?

5
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:20,190
I'll answer that question later.

6
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:22,010
But first, I have a question for you.

7
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:27,110
For how many of you is learning a process or

8
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:30,430
an activity that brings you genuine pleasure?

9
00:00:31,009 --> 00:00:31,650
Raise your hand.

10
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:39,570
And for how many of you is learning

11
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:43,770
more like something that feels like an unpleasant obligation —

12
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:45,470
useful, worth doing, but a chore?

13
00:00:53,870 --> 00:00:55,670
Raise your hand.

14
00:00:56,990 --> 00:00:58,330
For me too, sometimes.

15
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:06,910
What's interesting is that we can have

16
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:12,210
strong feelings about something, yet at the same time —

17
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:14,830
let me ask you a simpler question.

18
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:16,410
Do we even know what it means?

19
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:17,770
What does it mean to learn?

20
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:20,130
Well, I suppose.

21
00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:23,570
Please, go ahead.

22
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:25,590
To acquire knowledge.

23
00:01:27,010 --> 00:01:30,350
I'll come back to that point, but thank you for

24
00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:30,630
your comment.

25
00:01:31,750 --> 00:01:33,810
Same situation, different behavior.

26
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,050
Very soon.

27
00:01:38,810 --> 00:01:45,750
Let me now state a simple fact.

28
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:48,770
We know how to learn, we know what it

29
00:01:48,770 --> 00:01:50,370
means — but we have one problem.

30
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:55,250
Both answers to those questions are true — but

31
00:01:55,250 --> 00:01:55,990
we have one problem.

32
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:59,790
We only know this in a rough sense.

33
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:05,450
We simply know, more or less, what it means

34
00:02:05,450 --> 00:02:06,110
to learn.

35
00:02:07,289 --> 00:02:12,190
But I want to ask: to what extent is that

36
00:02:12,190 --> 00:02:14,130
truly detailed, truly useful?

37
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:16,070
To what extent do we really know what we're doing?

38
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:18,770
To what extent do we have a real map of how to

39
00:02:18,770 --> 00:02:20,190
get from point A to point B?

40
00:02:20,630 --> 00:02:23,010
To what extent do we have a map of how to get

41
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:25,830
from the bottom to the top — which, for a difficult,

42
00:02:25,930 --> 00:02:29,830
advanced, complex skill, is a very high mountain

43
00:02:29,830 --> 00:02:30,970
and a tough path.

44
00:02:31,770 --> 00:02:34,750
How and where do we get the confidence

45
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:37,970
that we truly have the right guidance

46
00:02:38,090 --> 00:02:40,670
to reach that peak, that high

47
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:43,310
level, that high level of skill?

48
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:54,260
We are more like people who, when asked

49
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:57,440
where China is, can vaguely point and say

50
00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:02,680
"well, over there" — or like someone who, when asked how

51
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,980
you want to climb that high peak —

52
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:12,200
simply says: "Just go up, keep climbing,

53
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:12,660
and you'll get there."

54
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:16,940
Would anyone, with that kind of mountain and that kind of guide,

55
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:18,200
get very far?

56
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:21,460
I very much doubt it.

57
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,500
Honestly — I personally wouldn't even

58
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:26,460
start those attempts if math is involved.

59
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:29,340
Now let's get to the specifics.

60
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:35,020
In the 21st century, we do have a map of

61
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:35,620
how to learn.

62
00:03:36,320 --> 00:03:37,580
We just don't use it.

63
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:40,580
In most cases, none of us even know

64
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:42,460
that such a map exists.

65
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:47,220
And this map was built over truly

66
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:48,820
the entire history of human civilization.

67
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,920
Just 100 years ago, we didn't have this map.

68
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:52,800
It was all shots in the dark.

69
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,600
We didn't know how to learn.

70
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:59,340
We had no real scientific research dedicated specifically

71
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:02,080
to how to go from the point of low skill

72
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:04,000
to the point of high skill.

73
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:05,220
Now we do.

74
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:10,380
That map is the life's work of a scientist

75
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:11,540
named Anders Ericsson.

76
00:04:11,540 --> 00:04:16,180
He devoted his entire life, truly, to working

77
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:20,160
with the many people who are absolutely the best

78
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:20,720
at what they do.

79
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:27,380
These people range from athletes to academics,

80
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:33,940
to Nobel laureates, to physicists, to practitioners of everyday professions

81
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:37,480
such as doctors and surgeons, as well as

82
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:40,240
entrepreneurs and business founders.

83
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:45,480
This is the life's work of this scientist, and simultaneously

84
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:48,760
the best map we have of the learning process.

85
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:53,200
And it comes down to diving into the details of

86
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:54,040
how one actually learns.

87
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:57,780
And above all, dismantling the myths

88
00:04:57,780 --> 00:04:59,680
about the learning process.

89
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:02,400
I asked those questions today

90
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:02,900
for this very reason.

91
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:08,140
When it comes to learning, the biggest problem we have

92
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:10,500
with what we believe about the learning process

93
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:13,240
is that we treat it as just knowledge.

94
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:18,540
And yet, knowledge alone is not something

95
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:20,760
that actually lets you do anything.

96
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:27,400
What's more, knowledge by itself

97
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:28,540
is useless.

98
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:32,780
What counts is skill — what counts is that we

99
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:36,040
are able to achieve a given result.

100
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:38,720
That we are able to genuinely do something.

101
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:43,620
Only then can we truly say

102
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:45,280
that we have any real knowledge.

103
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:49,880
True knowledge is always expressed through skill.

104
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:52,160
Now, as for learning itself.

105
00:05:52,930 --> 00:05:55,800
Learning is about how to practice,

106
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:57,560
and what to practice.

107
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:03,600
First, we must have immediate feedback.

108
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:09,960
Second, we must break down the enormous skill and high level

109
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:15,240
in any discipline into small steps.

110
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:19,360
And we must be able to place each step

111
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:22,900
at a precise point — a point

112
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:25,100
at which it represents the greatest possible challenge

113
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:27,940
we can still handle.

114
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:36,660
To close this talk, let me leave you with a final thought.

115
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:42,920
Let's develop skills, not just knowledge — and let's use

116
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:45,240
the map we have

117
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:46,100
on how to do it.

118
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:46,760
Thank you.
